---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '@/components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SupportingPage from '@/components/SupportingPage.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | SpellingWords.app"
  description="Learn how SpellingWords handles custom spelling lists, browser storage, shared links, speech synthesis, cookies, analytics, and children's privacy."
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath="/privacy" />
  <SupportingPage
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    intro="SpellingWords is designed to provide K–5 spelling practice without accounts or profiles. This policy explains what the website processes today, including how custom words and shared lists work."
    currentPath="/privacy"
  >
    <section aria-labelledby="summary-heading">
      <h2 id="summary-heading">The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You do not need an account or login to use SpellingWords.</li>
        <li>
          SpellingWords does not currently use Google Analytics or another site-analytics service.
        </li>
        <li>
          Custom practice words are kept in your browser's session storage while you practice.
        </li>
        <li>
          Shared-list links contain the words and optional title in an encoded—not encrypted—form.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not put a child's name or other private information in a word list or list title.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 25, 2026</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="information-heading">
      <h2 id="information-heading">Information the site handles</h2>
      <h3>Information you enter</h3>
      <p>
        You may type or paste spelling words and, when creating a shared link, add an optional list
        title. SpellingWords does not ask for a name, email address, school, account profile,
        payment information, or other identifying details. Please use a neutral title such as “Week
        4 Spelling” and do not enter personal or sensitive information.
      </p>
      <h3>Ordinary website requests</h3>
      <p>
        Like other websites, SpellingWords must receive a request from your browser to deliver a
        page. The hosting and delivery infrastructure may process ordinary technical information
        associated with that request, such as an IP address, requested page, date and time, browser
        or device information, and security or diagnostic information. The extent and duration of
        this processing can vary according to hosting configuration and provider practices.
      </p>
      <h3>Information not currently collected through product features</h3>
      <p>
        SpellingWords has no accounts, profiles, comments, public posts, purchases, advertising, or
        contact form. It does not currently use a site-analytics service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="custom-heading">
      <h2 id="custom-heading">Custom words and practice sessions</h2>
      <p>
        When you start a custom practice session, the words are saved in <code>sessionStorage</code
        >, a browser storage area for the current tab or browsing session. The practice-page address
        contains a random session identifier, not the words. SpellingWords does not save custom
        practice lists to a site-operated database.
      </p>
      <p>
        Session storage is normally cleared when the tab or browser session ends, though exact
        behavior and controls vary by browser. You can also clear site data using your browser's
        settings. If session storage is blocked, unavailable, or cleared, the practice session may
        not load.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="sharing-heading">
      <h2 id="sharing-heading">Shared spelling-list links</h2>
      <p>
        A shared link places its words and optional title after the <code>#</code> symbol in the URL.
        This part of a URL is called a fragment. Browsers do not include fragments in ordinary HTTP requests
        to the website, so opening the link does not send the list to the SpellingWords server. The list
        is decoded in the recipient's browser, and no shared-list copy is stored in a SpellingWords backend.
      </p>
      <p>
        Encoding is not encryption. Anyone who has the complete link can open it and see the words
        and title. A link may also remain in browser history, synced-browser data, messages, or any
        service used to share it. Share links only with intended recipients and leave out names or
        private information.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="speech-heading">
      <h2 id="speech-heading">Browser speech synthesis</h2>
      <p>
        SpellingWords uses the browser's speech-synthesis feature to speak words and sentences. The
        text is handed to the browser's speech system; SpellingWords does not send it to a
        site-operated speech API. Depending on the browser, operating system, selected voice, and
        device settings, speech may be generated on the device or processed by a browser,
        operating-system, or voice provider's service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cookies-heading">
      <h2 id="cookies-heading">Cookies, storage, and analytics</h2>
      <h3>Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        SpellingWords does not currently set application or analytics cookies. It uses browser
        session storage as described above. This policy will be reviewed before adding a service
        that uses cookies or similar identifiers.
      </p>
      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        SpellingWords does not currently use Google Analytics or another site-analytics service. We
        may add analytics in the future to understand general site usage and improve the service. If
        analytics is enabled, this policy will be updated before or when that change takes effect to
        describe the service used, the information collected, how it is used, any cookies or similar
        technologies involved, relevant user choices, and applicable retention practices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="services-heading">
      <h2 id="services-heading">Services provided by others</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Netlify</strong> provides website hosting and delivery.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Browser and device speech services</strong> provide available synthesized voices and
          may have their own data practices.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        SpellingWords may link to external websites for useful context or sources. Those sites and
        services have their own privacy practices, which SpellingWords does not control.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="children-heading">
      <h2 id="children-heading">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        SpellingWords is an educational website intended for K–5 students and the adults who support
        them. Its current product is designed to minimize data collection: no account is needed, and
        there is no profile, public posting feature, or backend storage for custom lists.
      </p>
      <p>
        Children should use the site with appropriate parent, guardian, or educator guidance. Adults
        creating lists should not include a child's name, contact details, school information, or
        other personal information. Keeping lists non-personal helps preserve the data-minimizing way
        the practice tools are designed to work.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="retention-heading">
      <h2 id="retention-heading">Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        Custom practice data is retained in browser session storage rather than a SpellingWords
        account or database. Shared lists exist in the links held by their creators and recipients;
        SpellingWords does not retain backend copies. No analytics retention period applies because
        analytics is not active. Hosting providers may process ordinary request information as
        described above according to their configurations and practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        SpellingWords uses data minimization and a static, frontend-first design to reduce risk, but
        no website or device can guarantee perfect security. Shared links should not be treated as
        secret or secure storage.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="changes-heading">
      <h2 id="changes-heading">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy will be updated when the site's data practices materially change, including
        before or when analytics, accounts, forms, cloud saving, advertising, or additional relevant
        services are introduced. The updated policy will show a new “Last updated” date.
      </p>
    </section>
  </SupportingPage>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
